        "notes": [
          "Zero violations in every same-code session: the violations floor is 0 events, so a single violation is never suppressed.",
          "depth>=5 counts spanned 15..28 across identical code, and depth>=5 is what the primary objective reads when violations do not move.",
          "h2 is nearly seed-invariant (2145..2153), so its floor is an order of magnitude below the relative non-inferiority margin.",
          "depth>=4 and h2 vary less than a binomial at the same rate (count sigma 8.4 vs 16.2 for depth>=4): the floor comes from configuration-level structure, not per-run coin flips.",
          "Measured at a tenth of a sequential chunk; the chunk-size band is extrapolated with the 1/sqrt(n) law, and four sessions pin the standard deviation itself only to about 40 percent.",
          "Worked example: a pooled comparison over 108000 runs reporting depth>=4 +1.53e-4, depth>=5 -1.48e-4 and h2 +1.02e-4 faces floors of 9.9e-4, 6.7e-4 and 4.5e-4 at that sample size, so all three deltas are inside the floor and carry no information."
